  "prefLabel": "Mil 201.07 Waiver or Suspension of Procedural Rules or Orders",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mil 201.07 Waiver or Suspension of Procedural Rules or Orders. The board, upon its own initiative or upon the motion of any interested person, shall suspend or waive any procedural requirement or limitation imposed by this chapter provided:\n\n(a) Reasonable notice is given to all affected persons;\n\n(b) The proposed waiver or suspension appears to be lawful, and would be more likely to promote the fair, accurate and efficient resolution of issues properly pending before the board than would adherence to a particular procedural rule or requirement; and\n\n(c) No party or intervenor objects to the waiver or suspension.\n\nSource. #7529, eff 7-12-01",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mil100-300.html"
